    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the clear engine of the offense. With an elite score of 80.61, he draws a favorable matchup against George Kirby; the high park factor and a projection benefiting from Kirby\u2019s reliance on the zone make **Gunnar Henderson** a must-start, especially given his potential for stolen base accumulation against a pitcher with a deliberate delivery. **Jackson Merrill** (75.26) also provides significant upside in the #2 hole against Singer, bolstered by favorable wind conditions that lift his power ceiling. Despite a difficult matchup against Luzardo, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains a staple in the UTIL spot, as his platoon advantage and lineup position maintain his efficiency floor well above the 60.0 threshold.\n\nConversely, our benching decisions were tight, specifically concerning **Brayan Rocchio**. He posted a respectable 46.62, coming closest to pushing **Dominic Smith** (49.52) out of the lineup, but the optimizer favored the platoon edge offered by **Dominic Smith** against Martin. We are monitoring **Nolan Schanuel** and **Josh Jung** closely; both are currently operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status. While **Josh Jung** carries a strong 60.24 projection\u2014aided by favorable wind\u2014any shift down in the batting order could deflate his value. We have already accounted for the scarcity of speed, ensuring that **Nasim Nunez** (56.32) remains active in the SS slot despite a middling base projection, as his utility remains high in our roster construction. Owners should remain cautious of the volatility inherent in today's lineup dependencies for **Nolan Schanuel** and **Josh Jung**.",
